{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CBNRbfttzJyyizshwofz12","type":"tool_result","content":"287:      \"review_profile\": {\n317:        \"resume_command\": [\n13:| `trn-43c6174032cb0775` | Passed qualification after encoding the absolute physical cwd in denyWrite: `go test -v -count=1 ./...` exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0; source, external and synthetic shared-metadata sentinels denied by the OS. |\n35:This is the vendor's shell sandbox, including test subprocesses. Claude itself remains a trusted executable with session/auth state outside this shell boundary; file-editing tools and hooks/MCP are not enabled. Claude can use its documented per-user temporary fallback when paths are long; this is not a claim of exclusive full-process confinement to one directory, arbitrary credential-read protection or a newly qualified engine containment backend. The shared-metadata sentinel is synthetic, not a destructive probe against this repository's Git database. Existing dispatch integrity checks remain the authority for the real sealed checkout. macOS and Windows have not been qualified here.\n16:The guarantee is Claude Code's OS-enforced shell boundary, including subprocesses, on qualified platforms. It does not turn the trusted Claude executable into an isolated engine backend or protect arbitrary credential reads. Existing checkout integrity and cleanup checks remain mandatory. A real execution must demonstrate permitted scratch writes, denied writes to sealed source, an outside sentinel and shared Git metadata, and actual traced Go test/vet execution. A configuration assertion or fake CLI is not proof of OS isolation. Linux is qualified on this machine; other platforms retain runtime refusal when the sandbox is unavailable and are not claimed qualified by cross-builds.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"e30027db-4b93-4e66-8394-25e9322b7806","timestamp":"2026-11-13T03:49:14.192Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"287:      \"review_profile\": {\n317:        \"resume_command\": [\n13:| `trn-43c6174032cb0775` | Passed qualification after encoding the absolute physical cwd in denyWrite: `go test -v -count=1 ./...` exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0; source, external and synthetic shared-metadata sentinels denied by the OS. |\n35:This is the vendor's shell sandbox, including test subprocesses. Claude itself remains a trusted executable with session/auth state outside this shell boundary; file-editing tools and hooks/MCP are not enabled. Claude can use its documented per-user temporary fallback when paths are long; this is not a claim of exclusive full-process confinement to one directory, arbitrary credential-read protection or a newly qualified engine containment backend. The shared-metadata sentinel is synthetic, not a destructive probe against this repository's Git database. Existing dispatch integrity checks remain the authority for the real sealed checkout. macOS and Windows have not been qualified here.\n16:The guarantee is Claude Code's OS-enforced shell boundary, including subprocesses, on qualified platforms. It does not turn the trusted Claude executable into an isolated engine backend or protect arbitrary credential reads. Existing checkout integrity and cleanup checks remain mandatory. A real execution must demonstrate permitted scratch writes, denied writes to sealed source, an outside sentinel and shared Git metadata, and actual traced Go test/vet execution. A configuration assertion or fake CLI is not proof of OS isolation. Linux is qualified on this machine; other platforms retain runtime refusal when the sandbox is unavailable and are not claimed qualified by cross-builds.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CBNRbfttzJyyizshwofz12","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
