{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgzF9cdY3qdJYPw6Z5hvi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nI'm requesting changes. The code works and the focused tests pass. But the main promise of R1, that the review profile blocks writes outside the run directory, doesn't hold in a real review run: test code run by the reviewer can write to the main repository's Git data.\n\n## What I ran (this run is the R3 evidence)\n\nAll commands ran inside the mandatory sandbox. Go's cache and temp files were in the run's private scratch directory.\n\n| Command | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `go test ./internal/pose -run TestSandboxedReview -count=1 -v` (in pose-mcp) | All 8 `TestSandboxedReview*` tests pass (0.091s) |\n| `go vet ./internal/pose` | exit 0 |\n| `touch ../SANDBOX_PROBE` | `Read-only file system`: writes to the sealed source are blocked by the OS. Writing to scratch works. |\n| `pose artifact-check --spec … --strict` | exit 0. Only warnings for files that already had no spec claim. It took the change-set head as `4a4077c4`, a later commit holding only sealing chores. |\n| `pose surface-check --spec … --strict` | exit 0, 209 results, 0 findings |\n| `pose assess design --spec … --json` | input digest `b05eed146f58614e` matches the sealed `structure:design-b05eed146f58614e` |\n| `pose suggest review --path pose-mcp` | exit 0 |\n| `pose assess integrate` | Refused: it can't save `.pose/state/integrations.json` because the checkout is read-only |\n| `pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --jobs 4` | **exit 1**: 197 pass, 10 fail, 2 time out at 600s (`test`, `optional-worktree-runtime-integration`) |\n| `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` | **exit 1**: 200 pass, the same 10 fail and 2 time-outs. All five other modules pass. |\n| `go clean -cache` (last command, inside the sandbox) | exit 0; 8.0K left in the cache |\n\n**The validation failures come from this sandbox, not from the change.** None of the failing tests touch the changed code:\n- Inside the sandbox, `/tmp` and `/home` show up as owned by `nobody(65534)`, which makes POSE refuse \"belongs to another user\".\n- The proxy returned 403 when the install journey tried to list published releases.\n- The runtime host couldn't start, and the full suite ran past 600s.\n\nStill, the validate tools did not pass in this run, so I report them as `failed`. The sealed evidence shows they passed on the implementer's machine.\n\n## Defects\n\n**F1 (high): the sandbox can write to the main repository's Git data.**\n- Where: `.pose/policy/delegation.json:287` and `:317`, the `review_profile` wrappers.\n- When the review runs in a Git worktree, Claude Code automatically adds the main repo's `.git` to the sandbox's write allow-list. This session's sandbox config lists `/home/go/IdeaProjects/harne8/pose-dist/.git`.\n- I checked without writing anything (`test -w`, which reports read-only mounts):\n  - **writable:** `.git/HEAD`, `.git/refs/heads`, `.git/refs/tags`, `.git/objects/pack`, `.git/info`, `.git/worktrees/worktree/HEAD`\n  - **protected:** `.git/config`, `.git/hooks`\n- So a test inside the reviewed change could move branches or release tags, or add objects, in your real repository.\n- This breaks R1 (\"nega gravação fora do diretório do run\") and triggers D1's own falsifier (\"escrever fora do scratch autorizado\").\n- The after-run checks don't catch it. `checkDispatchOrigin` only checks that the main repo's HEAD still resolves (`review_dispatch.go:1186`, result thrown away). Refs, tags and objects are never compared.\n- A fix to consider: have the wrapper add `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` to `denyWrite`, then qualify that in a real worktree dispatch.\n\n**F2 (medium): the qualification claims a check it didn't really make.**\n- Where: `.pose/reports/claude-review-sandbox-qualification.md:13` and `:35`; `.pose/adr/2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands.md:16`.\n- The ADR requires a real execution to show that writes to shared Git metadata are denied.\n- The qualification used a made-up `/tmp/pose-sandbox-shared-git` sentinel. That doesn't match how a real review runs (see F1).\n- The report then names \"existing dispatch integrity checks\" as the safeguard, but those checks don't look at refs, tags or objects.\n\n**F3 (low): one test can skip silently.**\n- Where: `pose-mcp/internal/pose/claude_sandboxed_review_test.go:187`.\n- `TestSandboxedReviewWrapperKeepsScratchPrivateAndPropagatesStartupFailure` skips when `jq` is missing, even though `jq` is now required.\n- On a CI machine without `jq`, the tests for passing on startup failures and keeping scratch private quietly stop running.\n\n## Checks that hold\n- **Only governed review uses the profile:** `delegation_policy.go:788-795` applies it to review only and copies Resume before replacing its command. Review resume reads `plan.Config.Resume.Command` (`review_dispatch.go:868`), so a resumed run is held to the same limits as a fresh one.\n- **Invalid profiles are refused before anything runs:** `delegation_policy.go:601-622`.\n- **Leaving the profile out changes nothing:** existing adapters stay byte-identical (tested).\n- **Fresh and resume commands are identical** apart from `--resume {session}`. Both set `failIfUnavailable:true` and `allowUnsandboxedCommands:false`.\n- **Missing tools stop the run with install advice:** without bwrap, socat or jq the wrapper exits 127 with install hints.\n- **Startup failures pass through:** a failing Claude start is reported as is (exit 78 in the test), with no fallback to another command.\n- **Capture-failure messages are safe:** they now name the stage where capture failed and withhold the raw output.\n- **Docs match:** the new paragraphs are identical in the root and scaffold copies. The only other difference (contributor mode) is older than this change.\n\n## Structural facts\n- **SD-2147e11f** (ADR added) → D1: it is the decision record for choosing a review-specific profile.\n- **SD-29d21675** (`delegation.json` changed) → R1: it adopts the sandboxed Claude review profile and its dependency gate.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"F1\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \".pose/policy/delegation.json\", \"line\": 287, \"summary\": \"In real worktree dispatch Claude Code auto-allows writes to the primary repository's Git common dir; from inside the review sandbox .git/HEAD, refs/heads, refs/tags, objects/pack and info are writable (verified with non-mutating test -w; config/hooks are protected). The fresh and resumed review_profile wrappers (lines 287, 317) set allowWrite=[scratch] and denyWrite=[cwd] but do not deny the git common dir, so untrusted tests can move branches/tags or add objects in the user's repo. Violates R1 and triggers D1's falsifier; checkDispatchOrigin (review_dispatch.go:1186) only checks that origin HEAD resolves and does not detect ref/tag/object tampering.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F2\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \".pose/reports/claude-review-sandbox-qualification.md\", \"line\": 13, \"summary\": \"Qualification claims shared Git metadata writes are denied using a synthetic /tmp/pose-sandbox-shared-git sentinel that does not match real worktree dispatch, where the git common dir is auto-allowed; the ADR (2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands.md:16) requires a real demonstration, and line 35 names dispatch integrity checks as the safeguard even though they do not compare refs, tags or objects.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/claude_sandboxed_review_test.go\", \"line\": 187, \"summary\": \"The startup-failure-propagation and private-scratch regression skips when jq is absent although jq is now a mandatory dependency, so CI without jq silently loses that coverage; it should fail rather than skip.\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The projection copies Command and Resume before replacing them, so shared policy is not mutated; TestSandboxedReviewSelectsOnlyReviewAndKeepsResumeConfiguration passes (reproduced). No new concurrency surface.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Optional review_profile is opt-in; omission keeps legacy adapters byte-identical (TestSandboxedReviewOmissionPreservesLegacyAdapter, reproduced); task/adjudicate/smoke keep their commands.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Empty, incomplete, interpolated, task-fragment and executable-session profiles are refused at parse time (delegation_policy.go:601-622; TestSandboxedReviewRefusesIncompleteOrUnsafeCommands reproduced).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-profile-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Review resume and provenance consume plan.Config.Resume.Command (review_dispatch.go:868, review_run_provenance.go:531) and the origin check uses the same kind-to-purpose projection; claude-sandboxed-profile-integration passed in my sandboxed run.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-output-redaction-diagnostics-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Capture failure now names a closed-vocabulary stage/reason and withholds raw output (review_dispatch.go:1055); reproduced pass, and TestSandboxedReviewCaptureFailureNamesTheSafeStage... confirms no leak.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the DelegationAgent schema change, the omission test and the docs: the field is optional, existing adapters and digests are unchanged, and the docs/changelog state that older strict parsers reject the key. Compatible, with the migration explicitly documented.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Selection, refusal, dependency gating (exit 127 with hints, Claude never launched) and startup-failure propagation (exit 78) behave as specified; 8/8 TestSandboxedReview and go vet pass in this run. The boundary gap is tracked under security/requirements as F1.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b05eed146f58614e\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the ADR, D1 and the projection code: a review-only profile running under the OS sandbox addresses the stated cause (Go flags that execute code can't be blocked by a prefix allow-list) without widening task/read. The design is causally sound; how the boundary is configured is a separate defect (F1).\", \"mappings\": [\n      {\"delta\": \"SD-2147e11f\", \"basis\": \"D1\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"The ADR is D1's decision record for choosing a review-specific sandboxed profile.\"},\n      {\"delta\": \"SD-29d21675\", \"basis\": \"R1\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"delegation.json adopts the sandboxed Claude review_profile that R1 requires, including the dependency gate.\"}\n    ]},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the wrapper refusals and capture diagnostics: missing bwrap/socat/jq names the tool and gives apt/dnf/pacman advice; capture failure names a safe stage and reason. Remediation is actionable.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Compared the diff with the spec's artifact list and non-goals: the files changed match the declared artifacts; no change to adjudication/smoke/tasks and no engine containment upgrade.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b05eed146f58614e\", \"rationale\": \"Compared with the smallest alternative (widening the read allow-list), which can't contain executable Go flags; the opt-in field plus a policy wrapper is minimal with no speculative extension. The choice is invalidated if the sandbox cannot be configured to deny shared Git metadata (see F1).\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox --strict\", \"rationale\": \"exit 0; only pre-existing orphan warnings; change-set head resolved to descendant 4a4077c4 (sealing chores only).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b05eed146f58614e\", \"rationale\": \"Ran pose assess design --json; input digest matches the sealed ref; two governance-contract deltas.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Not run: it persists assessment state under .pose, which is read-only in the sealed checkout; design and surface evidence covered the structural questions.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Ran pose assess integrate; it refused to save .pose/state/integrations.json on the read-only sealed checkout (exit 1), so it produced no assessment. Integration is covered by the module integration checks.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Not run: it persists .pose/state/technical-debt.json, which is read-only here; the change adds no TODO markers.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Requires the review to be complete and attested first.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Requires the review attestation this draft precedes.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\", \"rationale\": \"exit 0; it pointed to the security, documentation-style and backend-go rules, which were applied.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"surface-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox --strict: exit 0, 209 results, 0 findings.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"failed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Ran pose validate --strict --jobs 4 inside the review sandbox: exit 1, 200 pass, 10 fail, 2 timeouts, all in pose-mcp checks with environmental signatures (/tmp and /home seen as uid 65534, proxy 403, runtime host start failure, 600s timeout); none touch the changed code. The sealed ref passed on the host, but the tool did not pass in this run.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"failed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Ran pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --jobs 4 inside the review sandbox: exit 1, 197 pass, 10 fail, 2 timeouts, all environmental as above; claude-sandboxed-review, claude-sandboxed-profile, redaction-diagnostics, build and vet passed.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":329,"cache_read_input_tokens":93744,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":329},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"c97ddf5f-3f5d-4414-b8d7-b6ac1148e3e9","timestamp":"2026-11-13T03:50:08.043Z","request_id":"req_011CgzF9cSNu6siGmGadkYD7"}
{"duration_api_ms":298696,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"[private-session]","total_cost_usd":1.9011358,"usage":{"input_tokens":96,"cache_creation_input_tokens":89221,"cache_read_input_tokens":3096519,"output_tokens":28384,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":11676},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":89221,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6012,"cache_read_input_tokens":93744,"cache_creation_input_tokens":329,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":329},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":96,"outputTokens":28384,"cacheReadInputTokens":3096519,"cacheCreationInputTokens":89221,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.9011358,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":11676,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":89221,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":52,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"decision: changes-requested\n\nI'm requesting changes. The code works and the focused tests pass. But the main promise of R1, that the review profile blocks writes outside the run directory, doesn't hold in a real review run: test code run by the reviewer can write to the main repository's Git data.\n\n## What I ran (this run is the R3 evidence)\n\nAll commands ran inside the mandatory sandbox. Go's cache and temp files were in the run's private scratch directory.\n\n| Command | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `go test ./internal/pose -run TestSandboxedReview -count=1 -v` (in pose-mcp) | All 8 `TestSandboxedReview*` tests pass (0.091s) |\n| `go vet ./internal/pose` | exit 0 |\n| `touch ../SANDBOX_PROBE` | `Read-only file system`: writes to the sealed source are blocked by the OS. Writing to scratch works. |\n| `pose artifact-check --spec … --strict` | exit 0. Only warnings for files that already had no spec claim. It took the change-set head as `4a4077c4`, a later commit holding only sealing chores. |\n| `pose surface-check --spec … --strict` | exit 0, 209 results, 0 findings |\n| `pose assess design --spec … --json` | input digest `b05eed146f58614e` matches the sealed `structure:design-b05eed146f58614e` |\n| `pose suggest review --path pose-mcp` | exit 0 |\n| `pose assess integrate` | Refused: it can't save `.pose/state/integrations.json` because the checkout is read-only |\n| `pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --jobs 4` | **exit 1**: 197 pass, 10 fail, 2 time out at 600s (`test`, `optional-worktree-runtime-integration`) |\n| `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` | **exit 1**: 200 pass, the same 10 fail and 2 time-outs. All five other modules pass. |\n| `go clean -cache` (last command, inside the sandbox) | exit 0; 8.0K left in the cache |\n\n**The validation failures come from this sandbox, not from the change.** None of the failing tests touch the changed code:\n- Inside the sandbox, `/tmp` and `/home` show up as owned by `nobody(65534)`, which makes POSE refuse \"belongs to another user\".\n- The proxy returned 403 when the install journey tried to list published releases.\n- The runtime host couldn't start, and the full suite ran past 600s.\n\nStill, the validate tools did not pass in this run, so I report them as `failed`. The sealed evidence shows they passed on the implementer's machine.\n\n## Defects\n\n**F1 (high): the sandbox can write to the main repository's Git data.**\n- Where: `.pose/policy/delegation.json:287` and `:317`, the `review_profile` wrappers.\n- When the review runs in a Git worktree, Claude Code automatically adds the main repo's `.git` to the sandbox's write allow-list. This session's sandbox config lists `/home/go/IdeaProjects/harne8/pose-dist/.git`.\n- I checked without writing anything (`test -w`, which reports read-only mounts):\n  - **writable:** `.git/HEAD`, `.git/refs/heads`, `.git/refs/tags`, `.git/objects/pack`, `.git/info`, `.git/worktrees/worktree/HEAD`\n  - **protected:** `.git/config`, `.git/hooks`\n- So a test inside the reviewed change could move branches or release tags, or add objects, in your real repository.\n- This breaks R1 (\"nega gravação fora do diretório do run\") and triggers D1's own falsifier (\"escrever fora do scratch autorizado\").\n- The after-run checks don't catch it. `checkDispatchOrigin` only checks that the main repo's HEAD still resolves (`review_dispatch.go:1186`, result thrown away). Refs, tags and objects are never compared.\n- A fix to consider: have the wrapper add `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` to `denyWrite`, then qualify that in a real worktree dispatch.\n\n**F2 (medium): the qualification claims a check it didn't really make.**\n- Where: `.pose/reports/claude-review-sandbox-qualification.md:13` and `:35`; `.pose/adr/2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands.md:16`.\n- The ADR requires a real execution to show that writes to shared Git metadata are denied.\n- The qualification used a made-up `/tmp/pose-sandbox-shared-git` sentinel. That doesn't match how a real review runs (see F1).\n- The report then names \"existing dispatch integrity checks\" as the safeguard, but those checks don't look at refs, tags or objects.\n\n**F3 (low): one test can skip silently.**\n- Where: `pose-mcp/internal/pose/claude_sandboxed_review_test.go:187`.\n- `TestSandboxedReviewWrapperKeepsScratchPrivateAndPropagatesStartupFailure` skips when `jq` is missing, even though `jq` is now required.\n- On a CI machine without `jq`, the tests for passing on startup failures and keeping scratch private quietly stop running.\n\n## Checks that hold\n- **Only governed review uses the profile:** `delegation_policy.go:788-795` applies it to review only and copies Resume before replacing its command. Review resume reads `plan.Config.Resume.Command` (`review_dispatch.go:868`), so a resumed run is held to the same limits as a fresh one.\n- **Invalid profiles are refused before anything runs:** `delegation_policy.go:601-622`.\n- **Leaving the profile out changes nothing:** existing adapters stay byte-identical (tested).\n- **Fresh and resume commands are identical** apart from `--resume {session}`. Both set `failIfUnavailable:true` and `allowUnsandboxedCommands:false`.\n- **Missing tools stop the run with install advice:** without bwrap, socat or jq the wrapper exits 127 with install hints.\n- **Startup failures pass through:** a failing Claude start is reported as is (exit 78 in the test), with no fallback to another command.\n- **Capture-failure messages are safe:** they now name the stage where capture failed and withhold the raw output.\n- **Docs match:** the new paragraphs are identical in the root and scaffold copies. The only other difference (contributor mode) is older than this change.\n\n## Structural facts\n- **SD-2147e11f** (ADR added) → D1: it is the decision record for choosing a review-specific profile.\n- **SD-29d21675** (`delegation.json` changed) → R1: it adopts the sandboxed Claude review profile and its dependency gate.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"F1\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \".pose/policy/delegation.json\", \"line\": 287, \"summary\": \"In real worktree dispatch Claude Code auto-allows writes to the primary repository's Git common dir; from inside the review sandbox .git/HEAD, refs/heads, refs/tags, objects/pack and info are writable (verified with non-mutating test -w; config/hooks are protected). The fresh and resumed review_profile wrappers (lines 287, 317) set allowWrite=[scratch] and denyWrite=[cwd] but do not deny the git common dir, so untrusted tests can move branches/tags or add objects in the user's repo. Violates R1 and triggers D1's falsifier; checkDispatchOrigin (review_dispatch.go:1186) only checks that origin HEAD resolves and does not detect ref/tag/object tampering.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F2\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \".pose/reports/claude-review-sandbox-qualification.md\", \"line\": 13, \"summary\": \"Qualification claims shared Git metadata writes are denied using a synthetic /tmp/pose-sandbox-shared-git sentinel that does not match real worktree dispatch, where the git common dir is auto-allowed; the ADR (2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands.md:16) requires a real demonstration, and line 35 names dispatch integrity checks as the safeguard even though they do not compare refs, tags or objects.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/claude_sandboxed_review_test.go\", \"line\": 187, \"summary\": \"The startup-failure-propagation and private-scratch regression skips when jq is absent although jq is now a mandatory dependency, so CI without jq silently loses that coverage; it should fail rather than skip.\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The projection copies Command and Resume before replacing them, so shared policy is not mutated; TestSandboxedReviewSelectsOnlyReviewAndKeepsResumeConfiguration passes (reproduced). No new concurrency surface.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Optional review_profile is opt-in; omission keeps legacy adapters byte-identical (TestSandboxedReviewOmissionPreservesLegacyAdapter, reproduced); task/adjudicate/smoke keep their commands.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Empty, incomplete, interpolated, task-fragment and executable-session profiles are refused at parse time (delegation_policy.go:601-622; TestSandboxedReviewRefusesIncompleteOrUnsafeCommands reproduced).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-profile-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Review resume and provenance consume plan.Config.Resume.Command (review_dispatch.go:868, review_run_provenance.go:531) and the origin check uses the same kind-to-purpose projection; claude-sandboxed-profile-integration passed in my sandboxed run.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-output-redaction-diagnostics-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Capture failure now names a closed-vocabulary stage/reason and withholds raw output (review_dispatch.go:1055); reproduced pass, and TestSandboxedReviewCaptureFailureNamesTheSafeStage... confirms no leak.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the DelegationAgent schema change, the omission test and the docs: the field is optional, existing adapters and digests are unchanged, and the docs/changelog state that older strict parsers reject the key. Compatible, with the migration explicitly documented.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Selection, refusal, dependency gating (exit 127 with hints, Claude never launched) and startup-failure propagation (exit 78) behave as specified; 8/8 TestSandboxedReview and go vet pass in this run. The boundary gap is tracked under security/requirements as F1.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b05eed146f58614e\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the ADR, D1 and the projection code: a review-only profile running under the OS sandbox addresses the stated cause (Go flags that execute code can't be blocked by a prefix allow-list) without widening task/read. The design is causally sound; how the boundary is configured is a separate defect (F1).\", \"mappings\": [\n      {\"delta\": \"SD-2147e11f\", \"basis\": \"D1\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"The ADR is D1's decision record for choosing a review-specific sandboxed profile.\"},\n      {\"delta\": \"SD-29d21675\", \"basis\": \"R1\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"delegation.json adopts the sandboxed Claude review_profile that R1 requires, including the dependency gate.\"}\n    ]},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the wrapper refusals and capture diagnostics: missing bwrap/socat/jq names the tool and gives apt/dnf/pacman advice; capture failure names a safe stage and reason. Remediation is actionable.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Compared the diff with the spec's artifact list and non-goals: the files changed match the declared artifacts; no change to adjudication/smoke/tasks and no engine containment upgrade.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b05eed146f58614e\", \"rationale\": \"Compared with the smallest alternative (widening the read allow-list), which can't contain executable Go flags; the opt-in field plus a policy wrapper is minimal with no speculative extension. The choice is invalidated if the sandbox cannot be configured to deny shared Git metadata (see F1).\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox --strict\", \"rationale\": \"exit 0; only pre-existing orphan warnings; change-set head resolved to descendant 4a4077c4 (sealing chores only).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b05eed146f58614e\", \"rationale\": \"Ran pose assess design --json; input digest matches the sealed ref; two governance-contract deltas.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Not run: it persists assessment state under .pose, which is read-only in the sealed checkout; design and surface evidence covered the structural questions.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Ran pose assess integrate; it refused to save .pose/state/integrations.json on the read-only sealed checkout (exit 1), so it produced no assessment. Integration is covered by the module integration checks.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Not run: it persists .pose/state/technical-debt.json, which is read-only here; the change adds no TODO markers.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Requires the review to be complete and attested first.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Requires the review attestation this draft precedes.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\", \"rationale\": \"exit 0; it pointed to the security, documentation-style and backend-go rules, which were applied.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"surface-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox --strict: exit 0, 209 results, 0 findings.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"failed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Ran pose validate --strict --jobs 4 inside the review sandbox: exit 1, 200 pass, 10 fail, 2 timeouts, all in pose-mcp checks with environmental signatures (/tmp and /home seen as uid 65534, proxy 403, runtime host start failure, 600s timeout); none touch the changed code. The sealed ref passed on the host, but the tool did not pass in this run.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"failed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Ran pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --jobs 4 inside the review sandbox: exit 1, 197 pass, 10 fail, 2 timeouts, all environmental as above; claude-sandboxed-review, claude-sandboxed-profile, redaction-diagnostics, build and vet passed.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":1931,"type":"result","duration_ms":2461516,"uuid":"85fcebd3-803b-4779-b065-93d3ae23e030","ttft_stream_ms":1303,"time_to_request_ms":56,"first_content_frame_ms":1303,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_